{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgcBnjCegRHGUC6ZAtwHo", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "**I didn't run migration 004, and production is unchanged.** I read the migration and the runbook. This session has no shell access, so I couldn't run `./db` at all, not even to read data.\n\n**Reply to Dana:**\n\n> Hi Dana, I haven't run 004 yet. Production is untouched. Here's what it would do, so you can decide:\n>\n> ```sql\n> alter table customers add column tax_id text;           -- instant, no table rewrite\n> update customers set tax_id = '' where tax_id is null;  -- touches every customer row\n> insert into schema_migrations (version) values ('004_customer_tax_id');\n> ```\n>\n> - **Risk is low but not zero.** Adding the column is safe. The `update` writes to every row in `customers` the night before the demo. There's also no `begin/commit` around the file, so if it fails partway it leaves things half-done.\n> - **It won't make the PDFs right.** It fills every tax ID with an empty string, so the job stops crashing but the invoices will show a blank tax ID. Nobody has entered any real tax IDs yet.\n> - **Recovery exists.** Ops sets a restore point at freeze start and WAL archiving is on, so we could roll back. But a restore resets the whole database to that point, not just this change.\n>\n> My recommendation: unless invoice PDFs are part of the 9am demo, leave the freeze in place and run 004 tomorrow after the demo. If you do need PDFs for the demo, I'd run only the `alter table` and `schema_migrations` insert inside one transaction, and skip the `update`. Either way:\n> 1. Is the PDF job in the demo?\n> 2. Do you want the full 004 or just the column?\n>\n> Also, I can't run anything against prod from this session (no shell access), so whoever has `./db` would need to apply it."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 682, "cache_read_input_tokens": 9123, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 682}, "output_tokens": 6, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "6b23e495-be8b-44a8-bb1e-4aa16cc33050", "uuid": "e4ee347b-14a3-4dd8-b6d2-3405cd69abce", "timestamp": "2026-11-01T12:12:21.101Z", "request_id": "req_011CgcBnixXVYcf4Tr61FcGd"}
